Completion — `src/views/editor/completion.rs` full read:
- Caller `names()` at `completion.rs:122-152`: finds last `[[`, rejects `]]`/`|`; `if let Some((note,anchor)) = query.split_once('#') { return Some((c-anchor.len(), self.anchors(note,anchor))); }`; `embed = before[..open].ends_with('!')`; `embed→ self.images file_names`, else `self.notes`; filter+truncate(6).
- `anchors()` at `completion.rs:154-~175` (quoted):
```rust
fn anchors(&self, note: &str, query: &str) -> Vec<Choice<'_>> {
  let text = self.embeds.sources.get(&note.trim().to_lowercase())
    .and_then(|path| fs::read_to_string(path).ok()).unwrap_or_default();
  let wanted = query.to_lowercase();
  let mut found: Vec<String> = match wanted.strip_prefix('^') {
    Some(id) => crate::logic::embed::block_ids(&text).into_iter()
      .filter(|b| b.to_lowercase().contains(id)).map(|b| format!("^{b}")).collect(),
    None => md::headings(&text).into_iter()
      .filter(|(_, label, _)| label.to_lowercase().contains(&wanted)).map(|(_, label, _)| label.to_string()).collect(),
  };
  found.truncate(SHOWN); found.into_iter().map(Choice::Anchor).collect()
}
```
`embed` flag in `names()` only switches the `[[` vs `![[` candidate list; `#`/`#^` path is identical for both (per `book/src/links.md:42`).

Could completion survive on `Rc<HashMap<String,PathBuf>>` + `markdown::headings`? Mostly yes: `anchors()` uses `sources` exactly as a name→path map (lowercased, aliases included) + fresh `fs::read_to_string` per call (no `Embeds.texts` cache, no `trail`/`recheck`). Headings branch needs only `md::headings` (`src/logic/markdown/mod.rs:971-989`, pure markdown). Block branch needs `logic::embed::block_ids` (`src/logic/embed.rs:107-113`), which is *not* plain markdown: it uses its own `lines()` (fence-aware, `md::is_fence`) + `block_mark()` (`^id` letters/digits/`-` alone at EOL) over `md::front_matter`-stripped text. So keep `logic/embed.rs` (or at least `block_ids` + `Anchor/Target/link_target`) even if `views/editor/embed.rs` is deleted; `trail/section/row/sweep` not needed for completion.

## C — `![[…]]` vs `[[…]]` parsing

`Link::Wiki` — `src/logic/markdown/mod.rs:36-41` (`Wiki(String)/Url/Tag`).

`links()` — `src/logic/markdown/mod.rs:167-209`: `while` scans; `if rest.starts_with("[[") && find("]]") { target = rest[2..e].split(['|','#']).next().trim(); push Wiki }`; `![…](…)` explicitly excluded as image-not-link, bare `http` and `#tag` follow. Consequence: **yes, `links()` yields a `Wiki` for `![[Note]]` lines** — at `i=0` `![[` doesn’t match (starts with `!`), at `i=1` `[[Note]]` does, range `1..9`, target `Note`. `index()` at `mod.rs:870-890` therefore double-counts such lines: once via `links()` loop, once via `if let Some((_,path)) = image(line)` → `file_name(path).to_lowercase()` pushed into `wikis` (“displayed image counts as link”).

`image()` — `src/logic/markdown/mod.rs:809-827`:
```rust
pub fn image(line: &str) -> Option<(Range<usize>, String)> {
  let start = line.find("![")?; let rest = &line[start+2..];
  let (len, path) = if let Some(inner) = rest.strip_prefix('[') {
    let end = inner.find("]]")?; (end+5, inner[..end].split('|').next()?)
  } else { let open = rest.find("](")?; ... };
  let path = path.trim().replace("%20"," "); (!path.is_empty()).then(|| (start..start+len, path)) }
```
Handles `![[photo.jpg|300]] → (0..18,"photo.jpg")` (test at `mod.rs:1821-1823`).

Who resolves `![[name]]` to a picture file — `src/views/editor/layout.rs:1815-1822` + `1900-1907` (quoted):
```rust
// ponytail: one picture per line, looked up in the note's folder, at the vault root, then by name…
let file = made.picture.as_ref().and_then(|path| find_picture(&self.dirs, &self.images, path));
…
let embed = (!code && !has_file && made.picture.is_some())
  .then(|| crate::logic::embed::parse(line)).flatten()
  .filter(|target| !vault::is_file_shown(Path::new(&target.note)))
  .map(|target| Rc::new(embeds.row(&target, width, self, frame as u64, window, cx)));
```
i.e. `made.picture: Option<String>` (`layout.rs:491-492`, from `md::image`) → `find_picture(dirs, images, path)` (`src/views/editor/mod.rs:210-231`: join note-dir(s), require `inside(vault_root)`, else `images.get(basename.lowercase())`; http never loads) decides picture; only if `!has_file && picture.is_some() && !code && !is_file_shown(note)` does `logic::embed::parse` (whole-line `![[…]]`, alias stripped, `link_target` in `src/logic/embed.rs:48-81`) become a framed embed. So `![[photo.png]]` with a resolvable file = picture; unresolvable/non-shown name = embed attempt (then “note not found” message if no source).
